1
00:00:05,180 --> 00:00:07,580
Hey, you guys. Hey, what are you doing?

2
00:00:08,360 --> 00:00:09,480
Figuring out our wedding plans.

3
00:00:10,080 --> 00:00:11,160
Funny. We were doing the same thing.

4
00:00:13,568 --> 00:00:17,780
It's really crazy. The hall, the dress, the food.

5
00:00:17,800 --> 00:00:19,840
I had no idea how expensive this was.

6
00:00:19,860 --> 00:00:21,400
Yeah, it is really pricey.

7
00:00:21,640 --> 00:00:23,180
I freaked when I heard the numbers.

8
00:00:23,340 --> 00:00:24,760
So, what did you two do about it?

9
00:00:24,900 --> 00:00:25,660
It was simple.

10
00:00:26,140 --> 00:00:28,220
I came up with some cost-cutting solutions...

11
00:00:28,360 --> 00:00:30,560
...wrote out a list, and Monica told me to go to hell.

12
00:00:32,360 --> 00:00:33,500
There's no way around it.

13
00:00:34,480 --> 00:00:36,580
Just accept that this is gonna cost a lot of money.

14
00:00:36,660 --> 00:00:40,000
I heard that weddings are, like, a $40 billion-a-year industry.

15
00:00:40,100 --> 00:00:42,720
Yeah. And I'm responsible for just, like, half of that.

16
00:00:45,340 --> 00:00:48,400
But really, it does seem like this money could be put to better use.

17
00:00:48,760 --> 00:00:49,540
Are you serious?

18
00:00:50,120 --> 00:00:51,600
Yeah. How would you feel

19
00:00:51,600 --> 00:00:53,380
if we gave all the wedding money to charity...

20
00:00:53,380 --> 00:00:55,460
...and we just got married at City Hall?

21
00:00:55,800 --> 00:00:58,280
I think it would make me wanna marry you even more.

22
00:01:01,140 --> 00:01:04,340
I gotta say, you guys, that's an incredible gesture.

23
00:01:04,440 --> 00:01:06,120
Maybe you do that next time you get married.

24
00:01:08,860 --> 00:01:11,820
No, no, no. The next time's gonna be Hawaii at sunset.

25
00:01:13,140 --> 00:01:14,420
But maybe the time after that.

26
00:01:16,153 --> 00:01:18,243
《老友记》第十季第七集  领养中心来家访

27
00:01:55,806 --> 00:01:58,296
- Hey. What's going on? - Hey.

28
00:01:58,430 --> 00:02:00,720
Our adoption social worker is coming,

29
00:02:00,764 --> 00:02:02,294
so we're cleaning the apartment.

30
00:02:02,340 --> 00:02:03,350
"We"?

31
00:02:04,625 --> 00:02:06,555
You know you don't want me to help.

32
00:02:06,600 --> 00:02:08,480
You can't have it both ways.

33
00:02:10,580 --> 00:02:11,580
Is this the person who decides

34
00:02:11,580 --> 00:02:12,920
whether or not you get a baby?

35
00:02:12,920 --> 00:02:15,680
Kind of. She's coming by to interview us and see where we live.

36
00:02:15,680 --> 00:02:16,900
And it has to go perfectly,

37
00:02:16,900 --> 00:02:18,580
because if she doesn't like something about us

38
00:02:18,660 --> 00:02:19,520
she can keep us off

39
00:02:19,520 --> 00:02:21,000
every adoption list in the state.

40
00:02:21,260 --> 00:02:22,380
Hey, maybe I should stop by.

41
00:02:22,380 --> 00:02:23,800
She could be a soap opera fan.

42
00:02:24,860 --> 00:02:25,780
It's very impressive

43
00:02:25,780 --> 00:02:27,200
when the little people know a celebrity.

44
00:02:29,215 --> 00:02:30,475
"Little people"?

45
00:02:30,885 --> 00:02:31,925
"Celebrity."

46
00:02:33,860 --> 00:02:35,280
So I think I'm just about done here.

47
00:02:35,760 --> 00:02:38,200
Unless you have any bad stuff hidden somewhere,

48
00:02:38,320 --> 00:02:40,420
like porn or cigarettes?

49
00:02:41,000 --> 00:02:41,560
What?

50
00:02:43,700 --> 00:02:45,380
- No. - Chandler.

51
00:02:48,980 --> 00:02:49,840
I don't,

52
00:02:49,860 --> 00:02:51,740
and I'm offended by the insinuation.

53
00:02:52,860 --> 00:02:55,300
So there's not a magazine under the couch...

54
00:02:56,380 --> 00:02:58,660
...or cigarettes taped to the back of the toilet tank...

55
00:02:58,900 --> 00:03:00,600
...or a filthy video in the VCR?

56
00:03:02,560 --> 00:03:04,120
I'll admit to the cigarettes and magazine.

57
00:03:04,180 --> 00:03:05,660
But that tape is not mine.

58
00:03:06,400 --> 00:03:07,200
It isn't mine.

59
00:03:07,760 --> 00:03:08,980
I guess we'll never know whose it is.

60
00:03:18,100 --> 00:03:18,760
May I help you?

61
00:03:19,080 --> 00:03:20,120
Yes. We're here

62
00:03:20,120 --> 00:03:22,740
to make a rather sizable donation to the children.

63
00:03:23,200 --> 00:03:24,540
Any contribution, large or small,

64
00:03:24,540 --> 00:03:25,460
is appreciated.

65
00:03:25,900 --> 00:03:26,800
I think you're gonna appreciate

66
00:03:26,800 --> 00:03:28,040
the crap out of this one.

67
00:03:29,080 --> 00:03:30,660
Well, this is very generous.

68
00:03:30,900 --> 00:03:32,480
And we don't want any recognition.

69
00:03:32,500 --> 00:03:34,320
This is completely anonymous.

70
00:03:34,360 --> 00:03:36,960
Completely anonymous. From two kind strangers.

71
00:03:37,140 --> 00:03:39,280
Mr. X and Phoebe Buffay.

72
00:03:41,320 --> 00:03:42,040
Well if you like,

73
00:03:42,040 --> 00:03:43,300
we can include your names in our newsletter.

74
00:03:43,460 --> 00:03:44,300
Not necessary.

75
00:03:44,320 --> 00:03:46,420
Buffay is spelled B-U-F-F-A-Y.

76
00:03:47,860 --> 00:03:50,700
And X is spelled "Mike Hannigan."

77
00:03:52,800 --> 00:03:55,460
Well, on behalf of the children, thank you both very much.

78
00:03:55,980 --> 00:03:58,160
I'm glad we did this. It feels so good.

79
00:03:58,180 --> 00:03:59,400
It does. It feels really good.

80
00:04:00,380 --> 00:04:02,300
Oh, look. And we get these free T-shirts.

81
00:04:02,880 --> 00:04:04,840
Actually, that's the shirt I wore to the gym.

82
00:04:06,720 --> 00:04:07,260
It's moist.

83
00:04:11,360 --> 00:04:13,500
Hi. Emma will be up in a minute.

84
00:04:13,560 --> 00:04:13,960
Oh, good.

85
00:04:14,560 --> 00:04:17,060
Hey, Ross, listen. I heard about you and Charlie.

86
00:04:17,200 --> 00:04:18,339
I'm really sorry.

87
00:04:18,359 --> 00:04:19,689
That's okay.

88
00:04:20,060 --> 00:04:22,920
I'm sure there are tons of other beautiful paleontologists out there.

89
00:04:23,420 --> 00:04:23,860
Absolutely.

90
00:04:23,960 --> 00:04:25,840
There was one. She's it.

91
00:04:26,260 --> 00:04:28,840
All the rest look like they should live under a bridge.

92
00:04:32,140 --> 00:04:33,780
So, what are you gonna do today?

93
00:04:34,260 --> 00:04:35,920
I was thinking of taking Emma to the playground.

94
00:04:36,100 --> 00:04:37,740
Oh, my God. What?

95
00:04:40,380 --> 00:04:41,680
Like I said, I was thinking of

96
00:04:41,680 --> 00:04:44,700
taking Emma to the Museum of Knives and Fire.

97
00:04:47,540 --> 00:04:48,720
Okay, look, Ross.

98
00:04:48,760 --> 00:04:52,280
I do not want Emma going to the playground.

99
00:04:56,570 --> 00:04:57,800
Because...?

100
00:04:57,880 --> 00:05:01,360
All right, if you must know, I had a traumatic...

101
00:05:01,360 --> 00:05:04,280
...swing incident when I was little.

102
00:05:06,340 --> 00:05:08,360
- Seriously? - Yes. I was 4 years old.

103
00:05:08,620 --> 00:05:10,100
And I was on the swing...

104
00:05:10,200 --> 00:05:13,780
...and then all of a sudden my hair got tangled in the chain.

105
00:05:15,820 --> 00:05:16,740
And to get me out,

106
00:05:16,780 --> 00:05:19,800
my mom had to cut a big chunk of my hair.

107
00:05:22,040 --> 00:05:24,300
And it was uneven for weeks.

108
00:05:30,840 --> 00:05:32,800
And you made it through that?

109
00:05:35,100 --> 00:05:37,460
I wonder who's gonna play you in the movie.

110
00:05:39,560 --> 00:05:41,140
Okay, fine, you can make fun of me.

111
00:05:41,140 --> 00:05:42,920
I do not want Emma going there.

112
00:05:43,200 --> 00:05:45,420
Claire Danes:美剧《国家安全》女主角

113
00:05:43,200 --> 00:05:44,880
And I was thinking Claire Danes.

114
00:05:47,200 --> 00:05:49,520
Look, I'm sorry to hear about your tragedy.

115
00:05:50,160 --> 00:05:51,980
But the swings are perfectly safe.

116
00:05:51,980 --> 00:05:53,520
And besides, Emma loves them.

117
00:05:53,820 --> 00:05:55,460
You should come, and you'll see.

118
00:05:55,820 --> 00:05:57,960
Those things go, like, 40 miles an hour.

119
00:05:59,620 --> 00:06:01,280
And there's that moment when you're at the top...

120
00:06:01,320 --> 00:06:04,640
...when you just don't know if you're gonna return back to Earth.

121
00:06:07,100 --> 00:06:09,520
Space is filled with orbiting children.

122
00:06:13,000 --> 00:06:15,260
Look, please, just come on.

123
00:06:15,660 --> 00:06:17,340
When you see the look on Emma's face,

124
00:06:17,380 --> 00:06:19,260
I swear, you won't regret it.

125
00:06:21,600 --> 00:06:22,820
- All right. - Good.

126
00:06:23,300 --> 00:06:24,520
You don't wanna be a mom

127
00:06:24,720 --> 00:06:27,480
who passes her irrational fears to her children.

128
00:06:28,400 --> 00:06:29,260
"Irrational," huh?

129
00:06:30,340 --> 00:06:31,440
I'll remember that next time

130
00:06:31,500 --> 00:06:33,220
you freak out about a spider in your apartment.

131
00:06:33,700 --> 00:06:35,300
That's the same. I'm sure there are 30

132
00:06:35,300 --> 00:06:37,100
different species of poisonous swings.

133
00:06:42,140 --> 00:06:44,080
Oh, my God. The adoption lady is early.

134
00:06:44,380 --> 00:06:47,200
Okay. Okay. Here we go. Here we go.

135
00:06:48,140 --> 00:06:48,880
Stand up straight.

136
00:06:49,580 --> 00:06:50,140
Big smile.

137
00:06:53,720 --> 00:06:55,460
Hello. Is this the Creepy residence?

138
00:06:57,040 --> 00:06:58,380
We're waiting for the adoption lady.

139
00:06:58,640 --> 00:06:59,980
But I'm glad you're here.

140
00:07:00,480 --> 00:07:01,580
I was cleaning this morning

141
00:07:01,640 --> 00:07:02,760
and I found this.

142
00:07:03,200 --> 00:07:05,900
I don't know if you wanna use it, but....

143
00:07:06,620 --> 00:07:09,400
Oh, this is so sweet of you.

144
00:07:10,000 --> 00:07:10,580
But you know what?

145
00:07:10,580 --> 00:07:11,780
I won't be needing a veil,

146
00:07:11,800 --> 00:07:13,380
I actually won't be wearing a dress at all!

147
00:07:13,400 --> 00:07:14,360
I told you,

148
00:07:14,360 --> 00:07:16,100
I am not coming to a naked wedding!

149
00:07:17,300 --> 00:07:19,000
No. We're not having a big reception.

150
00:07:19,200 --> 00:07:21,060
we took the money we were gonna spend on a wedding

151
00:07:21,140 --> 00:07:22,940
and we donate them to the children charity.

152
00:07:23,200 --> 00:07:24,300
That's crazy!

153
00:07:26,720 --> 00:07:29,420
I'm sorry. I can't imagine giving up

154
00:07:29,420 --> 00:07:31,080
my one wedding day like that.

155
00:07:31,340 --> 00:07:32,200
Well, we're different.

156
00:07:32,580 --> 00:07:34,480
I don't care about having a huge party.

157
00:07:34,920 --> 00:07:37,020
This is really nice for you, but....

158
00:07:37,100 --> 00:07:40,880
Oh, please. I put this on and I just look like--

159
00:07:40,880 --> 00:07:41,980
Well, radiant.

160
00:07:45,500 --> 00:07:46,460
All right, but who cares?

161
00:07:46,780 --> 00:07:49,000
I don't need a pretty veil and a fancy dress.

162
00:07:49,240 --> 00:07:50,980
That's right. You're making a commitment.

163
00:07:51,940 --> 00:07:54,680
You know, that's the same whether you do it at the Plaza or....

164
00:07:54,700 --> 00:07:56,980
- Where you gonna do it? - City Hall.

165
00:07:59,220 --> 00:08:01,020
Oh, that sounds nice.

166
00:08:02,400 --> 00:08:03,820
I was just there for jury duty.

167
00:08:03,820 --> 00:08:05,820
They've really spruced that place up.

168
00:08:08,080 --> 00:08:08,940
Okay. It's okay...

169
00:08:09,500 --> 00:08:10,600
I've made my decision.

170
00:08:10,900 --> 00:08:13,660
What I really want is a great big wedding.

171
00:08:16,380 --> 00:08:18,460
But you gave all the money to charity.

172
00:08:18,620 --> 00:08:20,160
Well, I'll just ask for it back.

173
00:08:22,280 --> 00:08:23,560
I don't think you can do that.

174
00:08:23,580 --> 00:08:24,420
Why not?

175
00:08:24,580 --> 00:08:25,540
This is her wedding day.

176
00:08:25,540 --> 00:08:28,300
That's way more important than some stupid kids.

177
00:08:30,160 --> 00:08:31,060
That's sweet, honey,

178
00:08:31,120 --> 00:08:32,980
but save something for the adoption lady.

179
00:08:40,360 --> 00:08:42,040
- All right, okay. Be careful. - Okay.

180
00:08:43,300 --> 00:08:45,300
Careful. Watch her hair. Watch her hair!

181
00:08:47,240 --> 00:08:49,380
Rach, she's got, like, three hairs.

182
00:08:49,380 --> 00:08:50,660
I know. I know.

183
00:08:50,740 --> 00:08:52,380
But they're just so beautiful.

184
00:08:52,540 --> 00:08:54,360
Oh, my God, I just pulled one out.

185
00:08:55,800 --> 00:08:57,380
I promise you she's safe.

186
00:08:58,340 --> 00:08:59,780
Watch how much she loves this.

187
00:08:59,780 --> 00:09:00,380
Okay. Okay.

188
00:09:00,380 --> 00:09:02,360
Are you ready, sweetie? Here we go.

189
00:09:03,960 --> 00:09:06,900
Okay, careful. Okay.

190
00:09:11,640 --> 00:09:12,740
She's smiling.

191
00:09:14,320 --> 00:09:15,940
Look at that, she does like it.

192
00:09:16,020 --> 00:09:17,420
See, I told you.

193
00:09:23,260 --> 00:09:24,140
Oh, my God.

194
00:09:24,820 --> 00:09:26,380
Look at her, she's a little daredevil.

195
00:09:27,440 --> 00:09:29,220
Oh, God. Let me push. Can I push?

196
00:09:29,360 --> 00:09:30,200
Oh, absolutely.

197
00:09:31,840 --> 00:09:34,120
Oh, God. Okay, get the camera.

198
00:09:34,120 --> 00:09:35,220
It's in the diaper bag.

199
00:09:35,280 --> 00:09:35,880
Okay.

200
00:09:37,160 --> 00:09:39,120
See? Scared of the swings.

201
00:09:39,220 --> 00:09:40,560
I bet you feel pretty silly.

202
00:09:46,480 --> 00:09:47,780
We're asking for the money back?

203
00:09:48,140 --> 00:09:49,440
It's for our wedding day.

204
00:09:50,140 --> 00:09:51,620
Now, is this guy gay or straight?

205
00:09:51,640 --> 00:09:53,560
Because one of us has to start flirting.

206
00:09:55,600 --> 00:09:57,460
You here to make another donation the same day?

207
00:09:57,800 --> 00:09:59,640
I don't think that's ever happened before.

208
00:09:59,663 --> 00:10:01,093
Gay. Go.

209
00:10:04,360 --> 00:10:06,200
Oh, my God, I love your shirt.

210
00:10:08,660 --> 00:10:10,700
The donation we made earlier?

211
00:10:11,480 --> 00:10:13,280
Well, we want it back.

212
00:10:15,060 --> 00:10:15,720
Excuse me?

213
00:10:16,380 --> 00:10:18,620
Okay, that money was for a big wedding

214
00:10:18,820 --> 00:10:19,740
we thought we didn't want.

215
00:10:19,840 --> 00:10:21,080
But it turns out we do.

216
00:10:21,260 --> 00:10:22,440
So you're asking us

217
00:10:22,440 --> 00:10:24,600
to refund your donation to the children?

218
00:10:25,340 --> 00:10:25,780
Yeah.

219
00:10:28,060 --> 00:10:29,240
This feels really good.

220
00:10:34,260 --> 00:10:35,360
I'm sorry. I am.

221
00:10:35,500 --> 00:10:37,460
But this wedding's just really important to me.

222
00:10:37,520 --> 00:10:38,600
Hey, it's none of my business.

223
00:10:39,220 --> 00:10:41,180
Besides, this is probably a good thing.

224
00:10:41,480 --> 00:10:42,980
We've really been spoiling the children,

225
00:10:43,000 --> 00:10:44,420
what with all the food and warm clothing.

226
00:10:46,860 --> 00:10:47,820
That's not fair.

227
00:10:48,460 --> 00:10:50,000
A person's wedding is important.

228
00:10:50,000 --> 00:10:51,300
And especially to me.

229
00:10:52,200 --> 00:10:54,260
I didn't have a graduation party.

230
00:10:54,260 --> 00:10:55,480
And I didn't go to prom.

231
00:10:55,820 --> 00:10:59,720
And I spent my sweet 16 being chased around a tire yard...

232
00:10:59,720 --> 00:11:02,160
...by an escaped mental patient

233
00:11:02,160 --> 00:11:03,580
who, in his own words, wanted to:

234
00:11:03,580 --> 00:11:04,640
"Kill me, or whatever."

235
00:11:06,860 --> 00:11:09,660
So I deserve a real celebration.

236
00:11:10,180 --> 00:11:12,840
And I'm not gonna let some sweaty little man

237
00:11:12,840 --> 00:11:14,680
make me feel badly about it.

238
00:11:18,620 --> 00:11:20,540
She could've been talking about either one of us.

239
00:11:27,620 --> 00:11:28,600
Hi, I'm Laura.

240
00:11:28,680 --> 00:11:30,340
I'm here for your adoption interview.

241
00:11:30,420 --> 00:11:33,020
Hi, I'm Monica. And this is Chandler.

242
00:11:33,760 --> 00:11:35,440
- Please come in. - Thank you.

243
00:11:35,820 --> 00:11:36,780
Would you like something to drink?

244
00:11:37,440 --> 00:11:38,300
Water would be fine.

245
00:11:39,260 --> 00:11:40,980
We're so glad that you're here.

246
00:11:41,680 --> 00:11:44,220
We're excited about getting this process started.

247
00:11:44,300 --> 00:11:46,600
Because we love kids. Love them to death.

248
00:11:46,900 --> 00:11:49,380
Well, not actually to death.

249
00:11:49,520 --> 00:11:50,720
That's just a figure of speech.

250
00:11:51,200 --> 00:11:52,900
We love kids the appropriate amount...

251
00:11:55,020 --> 00:11:56,520
...as allowed by law.

252
00:11:59,100 --> 00:12:01,520
- Your place is just lovely. - Thank you.

253
00:12:01,580 --> 00:12:03,880
Yes, this building does have a wholesome,

254
00:12:03,880 --> 00:12:05,000
family feel to it.

255
00:12:05,980 --> 00:12:07,760
I feel like I've been here before.

256
00:12:08,440 --> 00:12:09,980
Any other couples in the building adopting?

257
00:12:10,200 --> 00:12:11,800
Is that that couple on the first floor?

258
00:12:12,180 --> 00:12:14,160
Because we should get a baby before them.

259
00:12:14,820 --> 00:12:16,600
That guy tried to sell me drugs.

260
00:12:18,260 --> 00:12:19,060
But other than that,

261
00:12:19,200 --> 00:12:20,840
wholesome, wholesome building.

262
00:12:24,200 --> 00:12:24,960
What?

263
00:12:25,220 --> 00:12:27,720
I realized why I remember this place.

264
00:12:27,920 --> 00:12:28,940
Really? What is it?

265
00:12:29,040 --> 00:12:29,920
Oh, it's nothing.

266
00:12:30,060 --> 00:12:32,000
I went on a date with a guy who lived in this building.

267
00:12:32,080 --> 00:12:33,400
It didn't end very well.

268
00:12:34,660 --> 00:12:37,560
That wouldn't, by any chance, be Joey Tribbiani?

269
00:12:37,640 --> 00:12:40,040
- Yes! - Of course it was.

270
00:12:41,960 --> 00:12:43,280
We had a great night.

271
00:12:43,600 --> 00:12:45,040
In the morning, he promised he'd call

272
