289
00:13:30,920 --> 00:13:32,820
Ross. Oh, my God, are you okay?

290
00:13:32,820 --> 00:13:34,200
Son of a bitch!

291
00:13:38,540 --> 00:13:40,580
Oh, relax. I didn't say the F-word.

292
00:13:43,560 --> 00:13:44,080
Ross, see,

293
00:13:44,080 --> 00:13:46,180
I told you! Those swings are evil!

294
00:13:47,000 --> 00:13:47,440
That is it.

295
00:13:47,500 --> 00:13:49,340
That's the last time Emma is getting on

296
00:13:49,340 --> 00:13:51,160
one of those things for her entire life.

297
00:13:51,860 --> 00:13:54,020
No, no, no. Okay, it wasn't the swing's fault.

298
00:13:54,020 --> 00:13:55,100
It was my fault.

299
00:13:55,100 --> 00:13:57,420
And kind of that kid's fault.

300
00:13:58,540 --> 00:14:00,840
Who is still laughing. Nice.

301
00:14:02,200 --> 00:14:03,740
Come on. Can we just get out of here

302
00:14:03,740 --> 00:14:05,140
before somebody else gets hurt?

303
00:14:05,240 --> 00:14:06,780
No. Wait. Ok, ok. I have an idea.

304
00:14:06,960 --> 00:14:08,760
I want you to get on the swing...

305
00:14:09,780 --> 00:14:12,320
...and you'll see that there's nothing to be afraid of.

306
00:14:14,520 --> 00:14:16,320
I know what this is all about.

307
00:14:17,920 --> 00:14:19,540
You've always been jealous of my hair.

308
00:14:21,480 --> 00:14:23,400
