- Joey, wait-- - No!

426
00:19:28,800 --> 00:19:30,480
I waited a long time!

427
00:19:30,480 --> 00:19:31,400
I can't wait anymore.

428
00:19:36,080 --> 00:19:37,800
I'm sorry that you had to see that.

429
00:19:37,800 --> 00:19:39,000
I'm so embarrassed.

430
00:19:39,020 --> 00:19:40,120
Oh, that's really okay.

431
00:19:40,480 --> 00:19:41,960
Yeah. We totally understand.

432
00:19:42,540 --> 00:19:43,440
Dating is hard.

433
00:19:44,280 --> 00:19:46,140
Boy, you people are nice.

434
00:19:46,900 --> 00:19:49,340
And I've got to say...

435
00:19:49,860 --> 00:19:52,540
...l think you're going to make excellent parents.

436
00:19:57,240 --> 00:19:57,920
Laura!

437
00:20:05,280 --> 00:20:06,320
We're back.

438
00:20:08,240 --> 00:20:09,640
Are you here to take more money?

439
00:20:10,720 --> 00:20:12,720
Because I think what you're looking for is an ATM.

440
00:20:13,980 --> 00:20:16,060
No, no, we're here to give the money back.

441
00:20:16,240 --> 00:20:17,660
Yeah. Because you know what?

442
00:20:18,500 --> 00:20:20,120
It's all about the children.

443
00:20:20,740 --> 00:20:22,900
Although it's also about the wedding.

444
00:20:24,980 --> 00:20:25,480
All right, here.

445
00:20:25,720 --> 00:20:26,300
No. Oh, God.

446
00:20:27,200 --> 00:20:28,560
If I haven't said so already,

447
00:20:28,660 --> 00:20:30,060
sir, congratulations.

448
00:20:32,300 --> 00:20:33,280
Enough, all right?

449
00:20:33,620 --> 00:20:35,420
I'm stepping in and putting my foot down.

450
00:20:35,640 --> 00:20:36,420
As your future husband,

451
00:20:36,600 --> 00:20:38,460
I'm gonna make this decision for us.

452
00:20:40,640 --> 00:20:41,900
What do you think we should do?

453
00:20:43,480 --> 00:20:45,760
You know what. It's not your decision anymore.

454
00:20:46,200 --> 00:20:46,720
What?

455
00:20:46,740 --> 00:20:48,240
On behalf of the children of New York,

456
00:20:48,380 --> 00:20:49,540
I reject your money.

457
00:20:51,260 --> 00:20:52,460
But we're giving you this.

458
00:20:52,680 --> 00:20:54,000
And I'm giving it back to you.

459
00:20:54,240 --> 00:20:55,840
Come on. Consider it a contribution.

460
00:20:58,160 --> 00:20:59,660
Well, this is very generous.

461
00:21:01,200 --> 00:21:02,260
Please take the check.

462
00:21:02,460 --> 00:21:03,420
Have a great wedding

463
00:21:03,420 --> 00:21:04,820
and a wonderful life together.

464
00:21:06,040 --> 00:21:06,760
Sounds good to me.

465
00:21:07,280 --> 00:21:08,840
We can save up, come back in a few years...

466
00:21:08,900 --> 00:21:10,000
...and make an even bigger donation.

467
00:21:10,380 --> 00:21:12,740
Absolutely. And when you do, make sure you ask for Brian.

468
00:21:12,880 --> 00:21:14,080
- Oh, is that you? - No.

469
00:21:20,180 --> 00:21:21,060
Hello?

470
00:21:22,560 --> 00:21:23,280
Oh, hi.

471
00:21:25,080 --> 00:21:26,960
Oh, my God, really?

472
00:21:27,500 --> 00:21:28,840
I can't wait to tell Chandler.

473
00:21:29,220 --> 00:21:30,080
Okay. Goodbye.

474
00:21:31,460 --> 00:21:31,980
Wrong number?

475
00:21:33,420 --> 00:21:34,220
That was Laura.

476
00:21:35,400 --> 00:21:36,680
She gave us a great report

477
00:21:36,680 --> 00:21:38,460
and we're officially on the waiting list.

478
00:21:38,500 --> 00:21:39,400
That's great.

479
00:21:39,480 --> 00:21:40,880
Now we just wait for a call...

480
00:21:41,040 --> 00:21:42,120
...and someone tells us

481
00:21:42,120 --> 00:21:43,620
